                {
                  "phase": "grammar",
                  "type": "grammar_rule",
                  "content": {
                    "title": "Hedging and softening",
                    "explanation": "Hedging es suavizar lo que decimos para sonar prudente, educado y menos categórico. Es clave en negociaciones, en el mundo académico y en los correos formales. Recursos:\n• Frases introductorias: It would appear that…, It seems to me that…, There seems to be…\n• Modales: may well, might, could. That may well be the case.\n• Tend to + verbo: Our designs tend to bring in more bookings.\n• Adverbios: arguably, to some extent, roughly, rather, somewhat.\n• Negaciones suaves: I'm not entirely convinced, I'm not sure that…\n\nEn lugar de «You're wrong», mejor «I'm not entirely sure that's the case».",
                    "table": {
                      "headers": [
                        "Recurso",
                        "Ejemplo",
                        "Más directo"
                      ],
                      "rows": [
                        [
                          "It would appear that…",
                          "It would appear that your prices are higher.",
                          "Your prices are higher."
                        ],
                        [
                          "There seems to be…",
                          "There seems to be a clear link.",
                          "There is a clear link."
                        ],
                        [
                          "may well / might",
                          "That may well be the case.",
                          "That's true."
                        ],
                        [
                          "tend to",
                          "Our designs tend to bring in more bookings.",
                          "Our designs bring in more bookings."
                        ],
                        [
                          "arguably / to some extent",
                          "Arguably, that depends on the market.",
                          "That depends on the market."
                        ],
                        [
                          "rather / roughly / somewhat",
                          "roughly a quarter; rather higher",
                          "a quarter; higher"
                        ],
                        [
                          "not entirely…",
                          "I'm not entirely convinced.",
                          "I'm not convinced."
                        ]
                      ]
                    },
                    "examples": [
                      "It would appear that your prices are rather higher than your competitors'.",
                      "That may well be the case.",
                      "There seems to be a clear link between good design and trust.",
                      "I'm not entirely convinced."
                    ]
                  }
